            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> The buffer contents are intentionally designed to only have the filename, so that yanking/copying the names can be used for :!, commands, etc. However, adding virtual text or other decorations could be worth exploring.\n\nIn that case, can we use extmarks for highlighting?  To be honest, being able to match dir.lua colors to `ls` colors is more important to me.  It just seemed like classifier characters were the easiest way to achieve this since we already have trailing slash on directories and the slash is used to determine syntax highlighting in `syntax/directory.vim`.",
